{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOrnaments","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOrnaments\/Content-swift.enum"]]},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOrnaments\/Content-swift.enum\/tremolo(_:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"The tremolo element represents tremolo marks used to indicate a note or chord that is repeated","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"individually, or repeated alternation between two notes or chords.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"tremolo"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTremolo","text":"MXLTremolo","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLTremoloV"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tremolo","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLTremolo","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLTremoloV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLOrnamentsV7ContentO7tremoloyAeA10MXLTremoloVcAEmF","roleHeading":"Case","symbolKind":"case","title":"MXLOrnaments.Content.tremolo(_:)","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlornaments\/content-swift.enum\/tremolo(_:)"]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLOrnaments":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOrnaments","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLOrnaments"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Ornaments can be any of several types, followed optionally by accidentals. The accidental-mark element’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"content is represented the same as an accidental element, but with a different name to reflect the different","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"musical meaning.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLOrnaments","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlornaments","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLOrnaments"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLOrnaments/Content-swift.enum":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOrnaments\/Content-swift.enum","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Content"}],"abstract":[{"text":"One of the alternatives for Ornaments.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLOrnaments.Content","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlornaments\/content-swift.enum","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Content"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTremolo":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltremolo","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tremolo ornament can be used to indicate single-note, double-note, or unmeasured tremolos. Single-note"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tremolos use the single type, double-note tremolos use the start and stop types, and unmeasured tremolos use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the unmeasured type. The default is “single” for compatibility with Version 1.1. The text of the element"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indicates the number of tremolo marks and is an integer from 0 to 8. Note that the number of attached beams is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not included in this value, but is represented separately using the beam element. The value should be 0 for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unmeasured tremolos."}],"title":"MXLTremolo","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTremolo"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTremolo"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTremolo","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLOrnaments/Content-swift.enum/tremolo(_:)":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOrnaments\/Content-swift.enum\/tremolo(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tremolo","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"text":"MXLTremolo","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLTremoloV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlornaments\/content-swift.enum\/tremolo(_:)","abstract":[{"text":"The tremolo element represents tremolo marks used to indicate a note or chord that is repeated","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"individually, or repeated alternation between two notes or chords.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLOrnaments.Content.tremolo(_:)"}}}